<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Marshal Konev    unloading   corn		7,561     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     20,000</p>
<p>				     wheat	    19,344</p>
<p>S. Morzov	  unloading   wheat	     2,501     Europe</p>
<p>Ozdem		arrived     barley	    2,580     Europe</p>
<p>Volgodo 5039     arrived     barley	    1,762     Europe</p>
<p>Ayhan Bayraktar  arrived     barley	    5,000     Europe</p>
<p>Zhatay	     arrived     barley	    3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Orel 5	     arrived     rapeseeds	 2,600     Ukraine</p>
<p>Volgobal 116     arrived     barley	    2,969     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 180	7/10	 wheat	     2,868     Europe</p>
<p>Sormovsky 43     10/10	 barley	    3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Valzsky 37	 10/10	 wheat	     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Semen Rudnev     15/10	 sunflowerseed   1,000     Europe</p>
<p>Federal Calumet  16/10	 barley	   21,090     U.S.</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	21/10	 corn+soya	60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Sergey	     22/10	 sorn	     24,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  16,000</p>
<p>				     soya	     16,000</p>
<p>Golden Sea	 25/10	 barley	   18,000     U.S.</p>
</text>
